// 生成于 2026-08-09T12:48:10.872Z：184 个字段键（表名→列名映射见 Player.Core GameTableMap） Id ID Code Name Name Notes Item notes, usually left blank, does not affect gameplay Range Attack range, 1 for melee, varies for ranged weapons DamageCut Cutting damage value DamageBlunt Blunt damage value ChargeProfiles Ammo/charge profile IDs (chargeprofiles, the ammo types), comma-separated e.g. '6,31' Penetration Penetration level Type Attack type: 0 Melee, 1 Ranged Sound Weapon sound category: Melee/Punch, Claws, Club, Blade, Rifle, Pistol, Laser, Bow, Throw, Choke, Grasp, Bite Transfer Transfer property: Whether attack can be converted to item, e.g., bow arrows can be recovered. 0 no transfer, 1 transfer (arrows, slingshot ammo stays on enemy or drops) AttackerConditions Conditions during attack, used with conditions data, e.g., '211x1.0,NSE:42x1' Image Image/icon file name (varies by table: weapon icon, map sprite, etc.) Morale Default morale bonus from this weapon, formula: (1+morale)*(1+melee/ranged morale bonus)*weapon damage=actual damage WieldPhrase Text description when entering combat with this weapon AttackPhrases Text description when attacking with this weapon, multiple descriptions separated by commas X X-axis coordinate Y Y-axis coordinate Buys Whether player items can be purchased: 0 no, 1 yes RestockTreasureId Referenced treasure data, used with treasuretable. Note: Detroit C shop is an exception, uses treasure pool 3 StrId Item ID, e.g., '90.35' Success Text displayed in game after action succeeds, <us> represents self, <them> represents target Fail Text displayed in game after action fails PopUp Action description in game, shown in action selection screen ChanceType Triple format `0,range-tier,chance-coeff` (`0,7,0` = stealth class) UsConditions Required conditions for our side, minus sign means NOT, i.e., not in that state ThemConditions Required conditions for opponent, minus sign means NOT, i.e., not in that state PairConditions Effect this action brings to self UsFailConditions Conditions brought to self when action fails ThemFailConditions Conditions brought to opponent when action fails (all official data is empty) PairFailConditions Effect brought to self when action fails UsPreConditions Prerequisites for executing this action, format like '137,151,-143' (negative means cannot have that condition) ThemPreConditions Prerequisites opponent must meet SeeThem Exposure level opponent needs to be at SeeUs Exposure level self needs to be at AllOutOfRange Distance from all targets on field InAttackRange Attack range, possibly used to determine splash or weapon length MinCharges Minimum ammo/charge count (0 = unlimited) MinRange Minimum range requirement, -1 for full field coverage MaxRange Maximum range requirement, -1 for full field coverage AttackModeType Attack mode type: -1 non-attack action, 0 melee attack, 1 ranged attack HexTypes Map hex type (all official data is empty) Chance Chance to use this skill (percentage) Priority Priority, no effect on player, Bot only, which side's action triggers first in same turn Detect Chance of being detected when executing this action, 0 means won't be detected Order AI action ordering weight Fatigue Fatigue cost Approach Whether this action makes you approach opponent Offense Whether this is an offensive action FallBack Whether this action is a retreat action Retreat Whether this action is a retreat action Position Whether this action is a position action Passive Whether this action is passive Description Description text (meaning varies by table) ImageList List of image file names (comma-separated) Capacities Camp size, format like '34x26' TreasureId Treasure pool ID for this camp Alertness Default alertness value of camp (percentage) Visibility Default visibility value of camp (percentage), -0.05 means -5% WetTempAdjustMod Default temperature adjustment of camp HealPerHourMod Default recovery effect per hour from camp (percentage) SleepQuality Default sleep quality from camp (percentage), -0.26 means -26% ItemId Item ID, e.g., '10.3' PerUse Amount consumed per use PerHour Amount consumed per hour, mainly for electrical power consumption PerHourEquipped Durability consumed per hour when equipped, only for XM54 filter chip PerHex Amount consumed per hex moved Degrade Whether it degrades FieldNames Effect field list brought by this condition, e.g., 'm_fHealPerHourMod,m_fImmuneRestoreRate' Modifiers Specific effect values brought by this condition, corresponding to FieldNames Effects Effects brought by condition, e.g., SetImmunity, ArmorWound. Like 'ArmorWound=100,0.1,0.05' Fatal Whether it brings death effect to player (will getting this condition kill you) IdNext Next stage condition ID this condition brings, may be multiple comma-separated Duration Duration (hours) Permanent Whether it brings long-term effects (like medicine, cuts, etc.), true means won't auto-remove after turn ends ChanceNext Chance of this condition bringing new condition in next stage Stackable Whether this condition is stackable Display Whether this condition is visible DisplayOther Whether this condition can be seen by others DisplayGameOver Whether this condition appears in game over summary Color Condition color: 0 white, 1 red, 2 green, 3 yellow ResetTimer Refresh time, one rest in game equals one hour RemoveAll 1 = removes all states of the same group (surrender, cafeteria, etc.) RemovePostCombat 1 = removed after combat ends TransferRange Infection distance, -1 for no spread Thresholds Trigger threshold, currently used for legendary skill triggers NamePublic Name displayed before contact EncounterIds List of condition IDs triggered when encountering this creature, comma-separated MovesPerTurn Action points per turn Faction Faction ID AttackModes Attack mode ID, used with attackmodes, may be single ID or comma-separated BaseConditions Base conditions when creature spawns, format like '38=1,50=0.5' CorpseId Corpse ID (treasure pool ID) Activities Description of creature's activity pattern, possibly for notes only CreatureId Spawned creature ID, used with creatures table Min Minimum spawn count Max Maximum spawn count (too large value causes many creatures to spawn in same hex) Weight Weight (itemtypes: item weight, 50 = unpickable; creaturesources: spawn weight) Value Value of this data EncounterId Called encounter ID, used with encounters RemoveTreasureId Treasure pool ID removed at player's feet when encounter occurs Conditions List of attached condition IDs for this encounter, comma-separated PreConditions Required preconditions for this encounter, negative means cannot have that condition Price Money given/taken; option hidden when the player cannot afford it Responses Player response options during encounter, format like '=15x0.083x0x0x0,=16x0.083x0x0x0' MinimapHexes Coordinates displayed on minimap RemoveCreatures Whether creatures need to be removed when this encounter occurs RemoveUsed Whether this encounter removes your items ItemsId Item ID generated when this encounter occurs CreatureHex Creature spawn position coordinates, format like '0,0' Teleport Position player is teleported to when this encounter occurs, '0,0' for no teleport Editor Editor coordinates (ignored by the game) LootChance Chance of successfully scavenging items AccidentChance Chance of accident occurring (e.g., building collapse) CreatureChance Creature ambush chance Accidents Event ID when accident occurs (calls encounters) Loot Treasure type ID when scavenging succeeds LocBased Whether this trigger is location-based DateBased Whether this trigger is time-based HexBased Whether this trigger is hex-based Unique Whether this event is unique AIPassable Whether this event can be triggered by AI Area Position coordinates where this event triggers, format like '20,164,0' DateMin Minimum trigger time, format 'year-month-day-hour' DateMax Maximum trigger time, format 'year-month-day-hour' DictFactions Reputation relationship with other factions, format like '0=-100,1=1,2=-100' HeadlineText Headline text content TerrainCost Action points consumed on this hex VizLimiter Visibility reduced on this hex VizIncrease Visibility increased on this hex Passable Whether can move to this terrain: 0 impassable, 1 passable ScavengeInitialId Treasure pool ID used when first scavenging this terrain ScavengeItemsIdPerHour Treasure pool ID used when scavenging this terrain repeatedly CampItems Camp type ID LightLevels Light levels, corresponding to: dawn, morning, noon, afternoon, dusk, midnight, 6 floats DefaultCampId Default camp ID code, used with treasuretable ConditionIds Condition IDs brought to player when entering this hex RequiredProps Property IDs the recipe needs; '&' means AND ForbidProps Property IDs this ingredient cannot have PropertyName Property name, e.g., 'easily ignitable' GroupId Item category group ID SubgroupId Item category subgroup ID DescriptionAlt Alternate description text (e.g. for variant items) CondId Condition required to use this item SpriteList Sprite image list ({value}={id} format) ImageUsage How the item image is used MonetaryValue Item monetary value MonetaryValueAlt Alternate monetary value Durability Maximum durability DegradePerHour Durability lost per hour EquipDegradePerHour Durability lost per hour while equipped DegradePerUse Durability lost per use DegradeTreasureIds Treasure table used when durability hits zero EquipConditions Conditions brought to you when this item is equipped PossessConditions Permanent conditions brought to you when holding this item UseConditions Conditions brought to you when using this item EquipSlots Equipment slots, positions item can be placed on body: 20 left hand, 21 right hand, 22 back UseSlots Use position, 211 for direct self-use (like taking medicine) SocketLocked Lock property, items with this property cannot be moved by player Properties List of property IDs for this item, used for crafting and checks ContentIds Space property of this item, defines what items can be stored as container FormatId Internal treasure pool ID of this item ComponentId Component ID, used with treasuretable, for reverse-craftable items, items obtained by disassembling if acquired by non-crafting means Mirrored Mirrored, specifically for shoes SlotDepth Determines which clothing is on top when wearing multiple items StackLimit Maximum stack quantity SwitchIds Switch ID, used for electronic device on/off state switching Sounds Sound when picking up or putting down this item Definition Map definition data, terrain data composed of large amounts of numbers and commas SecretName Recipe's hidden name, used to distinguish human meat from animal meat, water toxicity, etc. Tools Tools required for crafting, format like '1x1' Consumed Items that will be consumed/degraded in crafting, format like '1x2+1x3' Destroyed Destroyed items, used for extinguishing torches, etc. Hours Action points consumed for crafting Reverse Whether reverse engineering is possible: 0 irreversible, 1 reversible, 2, etc. HiddenId Whether it's a hidden recipe, needs to pick up paper to unlock Identify Whether it can be identified, used with hidden name TransferComponents Whether recipe components transfer to the output (e.g. bowstrings) AlsoTry Other recipe IDs with different recipes but same result TempTreasureId Crafting result ID shown as ghost in result slot during crafting DegradeOutput Whether crafted item durability is related to material durability: 1 related, 0 unrelated Scrap Whether it can be disassembled Nested Whether generated items will be placed in simultaneously generated containers Suppress Suppress content generation from items: when 1, water bottles won't have water, guns won't have bullets
Deleted "{0}" — takes effect immediately; saving is paused for this session and resumes after a restart. Cleared all saves — takes effect immediately; saving is paused for this session and resumes after a restart. Restored "{0}" Restarting the game to load the restored save… Save tips: backing up and deleting saves never needs a restart. When restoring a backup — if the game was just opened and hasn't been played yet, it takes effect immediately; if you have already played or saved, restart the game to read the restored save.
